export const internalSdl: string = "\"\"\"\nThe console's API: the internal schema of the gateway (business book §6, §7,\n§11, §12).\n\nSessions are a DEMONSTRATION MODE, not authentication: signIn picks one of the\ndemo's people, as the engine lists them, and the gateway keeps who they are in\na signed, HttpOnly session cookie. The browser never sends a role. Every\noperation is authorized on the server from the session, following the book's\n§12, and the engine checks the same identity again.\n\nMutations that change something in the engine need an Idempotency-Key header,\nand one request carries one mutation. A business refusal (signing your own\nversion, saving over a newer version) is an answer, typed as a Refusal in the\nmutation's result; errors carry extensions.code: UNAUTHENTICATED, FORBIDDEN,\nNOT_FOUND, BAD_USER_INPUT or ENGINE_UNAVAILABLE.\n\"\"\"\nschema {\n  query: Query\n  mutation: Mutation\n}\n\n\"\"\"\nAn amount of money in the currency's minor unit (cents, pence), never a float\n(§3.4). Written as an object whose amount is a string of digits, so that no\nclient rounds it: {\"amountMinor\": \"579\", \"currency\": \"EUR\"}.\n\"\"\"\nscalar Money\n\n\"\"\"\nA wall-clock time in a market's time zone, ISO 8601 without an offset:\n2026-10-26T09:00 or 2026-10-26T09:00:00 (§3.7). Whether the market's clocks\nskip or repeat that time is the engine's to say.\n\"\"\"\nscalar LocalDateTime\n\n\"An instant, ISO 8601 in UTC: 2026-10-24T07:00:00Z.\"\nscalar DateTime\n\n\"A market's code, ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 in capitals: IT, FR, DE, GB.\"\nscalar MarketCode\n\n\"A plan's code: lower-case letters, digits and dashes, starting with a letter.\"\nscalar PlanCode\n\n\"A SHA-256 digest as 64 lower-case hexadecimal digits.\"\nscalar Sha256\n\ntype Query {\n  \"The demo's people, for the sign-in screen (§12.1). Needs no session.\"\n  people: [Person!]!\n  \"Who is signed in, or null. Needs no session.\"\n  session: Session\n  \"The console's home: what waits, what launches, what broke, who pays, what comes in.\"\n  overview(at: DateTime): Overview!\n  markets: [Market!]!\n  \"The plans of a market at an instant (now when absent), with their prices and where the money goes.\"\n  plans(market: MarketCode!, at: DateTime): [Plan!]!\n  \"The price list (§4); every market and plan when the filters are absent.\"\n  priceList(market: MarketCode, plan: PlanCode): [PriceListEntry!]!\n  change(id: ID!): Change\n  \"Changes, newest first, a page at a time (first: 1 to 100).\"\n  changes(filter: ChangeFilter, first: Int! = 20, after: String): ChangePage!\n  \"The simulation of an offer in one market against not running it (§6.6).\"\n  simulateOffer(changeId: ID!, version: Int!, market: MarketCode!, overrides: [AssumptionInput!]): SimulationOutcome!\n  \"The audit log, newest first (§11). The auditor's (§12).\"\n  auditEvents(filter: AuditFilter, first: Int! = 50, after: String): AuditPage!\n  \"Recomputes the log's chain; with an exported head, also checks that the chain still leads to it (§11.3).\"\n  verifyAuditChain(anchor: ChainHeadInput): ChainVerification!\n  \"The engine's launches, newest first, a page at a time (first: 1 to 100). Every role reads them (§12.2).\"\n  launches(filter: LaunchFilter, first: Int! = 20, after: String): LaunchPage!\n  \"One launch, step by step, with its incidents and the audit events it wrote; null when there is none.\"\n  launch(id: ID!): LaunchRun\n}\n\ntype Mutation {\n  \"DEMONSTRATION MODE: become one of the demo's people. Not authentication.\"\n  signIn(personId: ID!): Session!\n  \"Ends the session; false when there was none.\"\n  signOut: Boolean!\n  createOffer(offer: OfferInput!): ChangeResult!\n  createListPrice(listPrice: ListPriceInput!): ChangeResult!\n  \"A new version from the one the author started from; refused as STALE_VERSION when someone saved a newer one (§6.3).\"\n  saveOfferVersion(changeId: ID!, baseVersion: Int!, offer: OfferInput!): ChangeResult!\n  saveListPriceVersion(changeId: ID!, baseVersion: Int!, listPrice: ListPriceInput!): ChangeResult!\n  validateChange(changeId: ID!, version: Int!): ChangeResult!\n  \"authorReason is required when the simulated contribution is negative (§7.3, condition 4).\"\n  submitChange(changeId: ID!, version: Int!, authorReason: String): ChangeResult!\n  \"Signs the version and fingerprint the approver saw (§7.2).\"\n  approveChange(changeId: ID!, version: Int!, fingerprint: Sha256!): ChangeResult!\n  rejectChange(changeId: ID!, version: Int!, reason: String!): ChangeResult!\n  scheduleChange(changeId: ID!): ChangeResult!\n  cancelChange(changeId: ID!, reason: String!): ChangeResult!\n  \"The on-call engineer stops an active change (§12).\"\n  suspendChange(changeId: ID!, reason: String!): ChangeResult!\n  \"The head of the log's chain, to keep outside the database (§11.3).\"\n  exportAuditHead: ExportHeadResult!\n  \"\"\"\n  The on-call engineer runs a failed or refused launch again from the step\n  that stopped it, or a waiting one now (§12); the reason is optional: what\n  was done so that it can go through. Refused with WRONG_STATE for a launch\n  that is running a step, done or cancelled.\n  \"\"\"\n  retryLaunch(launchId: ID!, reason: String): LaunchResult!\n  \"\"\"\n  The on-call engineer gives up a launch that has not published: its change\n  is cancelled with the reason, which is required (§7.1, §12). A launch that\n  has published is refused with WRONG_STATE: suspendChange takes its change\n  off the site.\n  \"\"\"\n  cancelLaunch(launchId: ID!, reason: String!): LaunchResult!\n}\n\nenum Role {\n  MARKETING\n  COMMERCIAL_LEAD\n  FINANCE\n  CATALOG_MANAGER\n  ON_CALL\n  AUDITOR\n}\n\n\"Who wrote an audit event: a role of the book, the engine's own jobs, or a subscriber of the site (§11.1).\"\nenum ActorRole {\n  MARKETING\n  COMMERCIAL_LEAD\n  FINANCE\n  CATALOG_MANAGER\n  ON_CALL\n  AUDITOR\n  SYSTEM\n  SUBSCRIBER\n}\n\n\"A person of the demo, named by role, never by a person's name (§12.1).\"\ntype Person {\n  id: ID!\n  label: String!\n  roles: [Role!]!\n}\n\n\"There is no real authentication: every session is a demonstration.\"\nenum SessionMode {\n  DEMONSTRATION\n}\n\ntype Session {\n  mode: SessionMode!\n  person: Person!\n  \"The roles the session acts in, as the engine lists them for the person.\"\n  roles: [Role!]!\n  \"Send it back in the X-CSRF-Token header with every mutation.\"\n  csrfToken: String!\n  expiresAt: DateTime!\n}\n\ntype Market {\n  code: MarketCode!\n  name: String!\n  currency: String!\n  minorUnits: Int!\n  timeZone: String!\n  \"The standard VAT rate in force, in basis points: 2200 is 22% (§3.1).\"\n  vatBasisPoints: Int!\n  \"What every paying subscription pays into the artists' pool at least, every month (§5.3).\"\n  artistsMinimum: Money!\n  \"The lowest price whose pool covers the minimum without a top-up (§5.4).\"\n  floor: Money!\n}\n\nenum AudioQuality {\n  STANDARD\n  LOSSLESS\n}\n\ntype Entitlements {\n  \"Null means unlimited.\"\n  skipsPerHour: Int\n  audio: AudioQuality!\n  offline: Boolean!\n  seats: Int!\n  needsStudentCheck: Boolean!\n}\n\n\"Where a price goes, per subscription per month (§3.5, §5).\"\ntype PriceBreakdown {\n  price: Money!\n  vat: Money!\n  net: Money!\n  \"The pool share of the net amount, never less than the minimum.\"\n  artists: Money!\n  \"The part of artists that the company adds from its margin to reach the minimum.\"\n  topUp: Money!\n  paymentCosts: Money!\n  companyKeeps: Money!\n}\n\ntype Plan {\n  code: PlanCode!\n  name: String!\n  paid: Boolean!\n  entitlements: Entitlements!\n  \"Null for the free plan.\"\n  listPrice: Money\n  breakdown: PriceBreakdown\n}\n\ntype PriceListEntry {\n  id: ID!\n  plan: PlanCode!\n  market: MarketCode!\n  amount: Money!\n  validFrom: LocalDateTime!\n  \"Null: open-ended.\"\n  validUntil: LocalDateTime\n  \"The approved change that created it; null for the price list loaded at the start of the data.\"\n  change: Change\n  \"Below the market's floor: a standing exception approved by finance (§5.5).\"\n  belowFloor: Boolean!\n  \"What the minimum costs the company per subscription per month at this price.\"\n  topUp: Money!\n}\n\nenum ChangeKind {\n  OFFER\n  LIST_PRICE\n  ENTITLEMENT\n  PRICE_MIGRATION\n  PREPAID\n}\n\nenum ChangeState {\n  DRAFT\n  VALIDATED\n  IN_APPROVAL\n  APPROVED\n  SCHEDULED\n  ACTIVE\n  ENDED\n  SUSPENDED\n  CANCELLED\n}\n\ninput ChangeFilter {\n  states: [ChangeState!]\n  kind: ChangeKind\n  market: MarketCode\n}\n\ntype ChangePage {\n  nodes: [ChangeSummary!]!\n  \"The cursor of the next page; null on the last one.\"\n  next: String\n}\n\n\"A row of the list of changes.\"\ntype ChangeSummary {\n  id: ID!\n  kind: ChangeKind!\n  title: String!\n  state: ChangeState!\n  currentVersion: Int!\n  createdBy: Person!\n  markets: [MarketCode!]!\n  requiredSignatures: [RequiredSignature!]!\n  updatedAt: DateTime!\n  \"The whole change, loaded in one batch with the other rows of the page.\"\n  details: Change!\n}\n\ntype Change {\n  id: ID!\n  kind: ChangeKind!\n  title: String!\n  state: ChangeState!\n  \"Why it was rejected, suspended or cancelled.\"\n  stateReason: String\n  currentVersion: Int!\n  createdBy: Person!\n  createdAt: DateTime!\n  versions: [ChangeVersion!]!\n  \"The version that validation and approvals refer to.\"\n  current: ChangeVersion!\n  approvals: [Approval!]!\n  validation: ValidationReport\n  requiredSignatures: [RequiredSignature!]!\n  \"The difference in business words, before anyone approves (§6.5).\"\n  sentence: String\n  \"Why the campaign is worth running despite a negative contribution (§7.3, condition 4).\"\n  authorReason: String\n}\n\ntype ChangeVersion {\n  version: Int!\n  author: Person!\n  createdAt: DateTime!\n  \"SHA-256 of the content as the database stored it: what an approval names (§7.2).\"\n  fingerprint: Sha256!\n  content: ChangeContent!\n}\n\nunion ChangeContent = OfferContent | ListPriceContent\n\nenum Segment {\n  \"People who have never paid.\"\n  NEVER_PAID\n  \"People on the free plan now.\"\n  FREE_LISTENERS\n  \"Paying subscribers of currentPlan now.\"\n  SUBSCRIBERS_OF_PLAN\n  \"Anyone: a gift bought for someone else.\"\n  ANYONE\n}\n\n\"Free listeners who played an artist for more than a set time lately (§14.2).\"\ntype ListeningRule {\n  artistId: Int!\n  minSeconds: Int!\n  withinDays: Int!\n}\n\ntype Audience {\n  segment: Segment!\n  currentPlan: PlanCode\n  needsStudentCheck: Boolean!\n  listening: ListeningRule\n}\n\n\"The price of an offer in one market: a fixed amount, or a percentage off the list price in force (§6.1).\"\ntype OfferPrice {\n  market: MarketCode!\n  fixed: Money\n  percentOffBasisPoints: Int\n}\n\n\"When the offer can be taken in one market, in local time; no end: open.\"\ntype OfferPeriod {\n  market: MarketCode!\n  startsLocal: LocalDateTime!\n  endsLocal: LocalDateTime\n}\n\n\"The page of the offer in one market (§6.1).\"\ntype OfferPage {\n  market: MarketCode!\n  title: String!\n  text: String!\n  terms: String!\n  treatment: String!\n}\n\ntype OfferContent {\n  title: String!\n  plan: PlanCode!\n  audience: Audience!\n  prices: [OfferPrice!]!\n  monthsAtOfferPrice: Int!\n  periods: [OfferPeriod!]!\n  \"Offers in the same group never stack (§6.1, §10.3).\"\n  nonCombinabilityGroup: String!\n  \"Null: no cap.\"\n  redemptionCap: Int\n  pages: [OfferPage!]!\n}\n\n\"A new list price for one plan and market, from a local time (§4.2).\"\ntype ListPriceContent {\n  title: String!\n  plan: PlanCode!\n  market: MarketCode!\n  amount: Money!\n  startsLocal: LocalDateTime!\n}\n\ninput ListeningRuleInput {\n  artistId: Int!\n  minSeconds: Int!\n  withinDays: Int!\n}\n\ninput AudienceInput {\n  segment: Segment!\n  currentPlan: PlanCode\n  needsStudentCheck: Boolean! = false\n  listening: ListeningRuleInput\n}\n\n\"Exactly one of fixed and percentOffBasisPoints.\"\ninput OfferPriceInput {\n  market: MarketCode!\n  fixed: Money\n  percentOffBasisPoints: Int\n}\n\ninput OfferPeriodInput {\n  market: MarketCode!\n  startsLocal: LocalDateTime!\n  endsLocal: LocalDateTime\n}\n\ninput OfferPageInput {\n  market: MarketCode!\n  title: String!\n  text: String!\n  terms: String!\n  treatment: String! = \"standard\"\n}\n\ninput OfferInput {\n  title: String!\n  plan: PlanCode!\n  audience: AudienceInput!\n  prices: [OfferPriceInput!]!\n  monthsAtOfferPrice: Int!\n  periods: [OfferPeriodInput!]!\n  nonCombinabilityGroup: String!\n  \"Null: no cap.\"\n  redemptionCap: Int\n  pages: [OfferPageInput!]!\n}\n\ninput ListPriceInput {\n  title: String!\n  plan: PlanCode!\n  market: MarketCode!\n  amount: Money!\n  startsLocal: LocalDateTime!\n}\n\ntype Approval {\n  version: Int!\n  approver: Person!\n  role: Role!\n  decidedAt: DateTime!\n  fingerprint: Sha256!\n}\n\n\"A signature the current version needs, and why (§7.3, conditions 1 to 5).\"\ntype RequiredSignature {\n  role: Role!\n  conditions: [Int!]!\n  why: String!\n  signed: Boolean!\n}\n\nenum Severity {\n  \"The version cannot be submitted.\"\n  BLOCKING\n  \"It can, and someone will have to sign for it.\"\n  NEEDS_SIGNATURE\n  INFO\n}\n\n\"A name and a value that a sentence for people was made of.\"\ntype Fact {\n  name: String!\n  value: String!\n}\n\ntype ValidationFinding {\n  \"floor, overlap, conflict, dates, time_zone, audience, page_text or signatures.\"\n  check: String!\n  severity: Severity!\n  \"Null when the finding is not about one market.\"\n  market: MarketCode\n  message: String!\n  facts: [Fact!]!\n}\n\ntype ValidationReport {\n  version: Int!\n  valid: Boolean!\n  findings: [ValidationFinding!]!\n  \"How many people the audience reaches now, counted in the data, never typed (§6.5).\"\n  eligible: Int!\n}\n\nenum RefusalCode {\n  \"The author of a version cannot approve it (§7.4).\"\n  OWN_VERSION\n  \"The actor's role may not do this (§12).\"\n  ROLE_NOT_ALLOWED\n  \"Someone saved a newer version (§6.3): the refusal's change field carries it.\"\n  STALE_VERSION\n  \"The change is not in a state that allows this (§7.1).\"\n  WRONG_STATE\n  \"Another price for the same plan and market covers part of the period (§4.1).\"\n  OVERLAP\n  \"Validation found a blocking problem.\"\n  INVALID\n  \"This person, or this role, has already signed this version.\"\n  ALREADY_SIGNED\n  \"The approval names a version or fingerprint that is not the current one (§7.2).\"\n  FINGERPRINT_MISMATCH\n  \"A reason is required and none was given.\"\n  REASON_REQUIRED\n  \"A clock change skips or repeats that local time in the market.\"\n  AMBIGUOUS_LOCAL_TIME\n  \"The quote expired, or names an offer that is no longer in force (§4.5).\"\n  QUOTE_EXPIRED\n  \"The person is not in the offer's audience.\"\n  NOT_ELIGIBLE\n  \"A paid subscription of this listener is already running.\"\n  ALREADY_SUBSCRIBED\n  \"The listener already took an offer of the same non-combinability group (§10.3).\"\n  NOT_COMBINABLE\n  \"The offer's cap on redemptions is reached (§6.1).\"\n  CAP_REACHED\n  \"The payment provider declined the charge (the simulated one never does).\"\n  PAYMENT_DECLINED\n}\n\n\"The rules said no: an answer, not an error.\"\ntype Refusal {\n  code: RefusalCode!\n  \"One sentence for people.\"\n  reason: String!\n  \"The numbers and names the sentence is made of.\"\n  facts: [Fact!]!\n  \"The change as it is now, when the refusal is about one: with STALE_VERSION, the newer version.\"\n  change: Change\n}\n\nunion ChangeResult = Change | Refusal\n\ntype Overview {\n  waitingForApproval: [ChangeSummary!]!\n  launchesNext7Days: [Launch!]!\n  \"The incidents open at this instant, and those opened or closed on its day (UTC), newest first.\"\n  incidentsToday: [Incident!]!\n  payingSubscribers: [SubscriberCount!]!\n  freeListeners: [SubscriberCount!]!\n  \"Revenue without VAT this month, per market. Finance and the commercial lead only (§12).\"\n  monthlyRevenue: [MarketRevenue!]\n  \"The same in euros at the declared rate (§3.6). Finance and the commercial lead only.\"\n  monthlyRevenueEur: Money\n  \"What the company adds this month to reach the artists' minimum (§5.5). Finance and the commercial lead only.\"\n  monthlyTopUps: Money\n  \"1 EUR = 0.83728 GBP (ECB reference rate, 23 October 2026).\"\n  exchangeRateNote: String!\n}\n\ntype MarketTime {\n  market: MarketCode!\n  local: LocalDateTime!\n  utc: DateTime!\n}\n\ntype Launch {\n  change: Change!\n  title: String!\n  starts: MarketTime!\n  state: ChangeState!\n  \"Not approved yet: it will not start until the missing signatures arrive.\"\n  atRisk: Boolean!\n  risk: String\n}\n\n\"How an incident of a launch stands.\"\nenum IncidentState {\n  \"Its launch went through on its own, and nobody had to act.\"\n  RECOVERED\n  OPEN\n  \"A person retried or cancelled the launch.\"\n  RESOLVED\n}\n\n\"Why an incident opened.\"\nenum IncidentKind {\n  \"A scheduled change not live 5 minutes after its start: the alarm.\"\n  LATE\n  \"A step of the launch failed 5 times.\"\n  FAILED\n  \"The launch's check found a clash or a later price.\"\n  REFUSED\n}\n\n\"An incident of a launch (§7.5): a launch that failed or was refused, or a scheduled change not live 5 minutes after its start.\"\ntype Incident {\n  change: Change!\n  title: String!\n  \"The launch's run identifier, as its audit events and log lines carry it: launch-12.\"\n  run: String!\n  state: IncidentState!\n  summary: String!\n  \"The launch it is about; launch(id) reads it. Null for a late start the engine has not begun to launch.\"\n  launchId: ID\n  kind: IncidentKind!\n  openedAt: DateTime!\n  \"Null while it is open.\"\n  closedAt: DateTime\n  \"How it closed: published at ..., cancelled by on-call-1: ...; null while it is open.\"\n  resolution: String\n}\n\ninput LaunchFilter {\n  state: LaunchState\n  changeId: ID\n}\n\ntype LaunchPage {\n  nodes: [LaunchRun!]!\n  \"The cursor of the next page; null on the last one.\"\n  next: String\n}\n\n\"Where a launch stands.\"\nenum LaunchState {\n  \"Steps remain: the engine works on them, or waits to try a failed one again.\"\n  RUNNING\n  \"Published, the site told, the live catalog checked.\"\n  DONE\n  \"A step failed 5 times. Nothing was published unless its publish step is done.\"\n  FAILED\n  \"The check found a clash or a later price: nothing was published, and the change stays scheduled.\"\n  REFUSED\n  \"Given up before it published: its change is cancelled.\"\n  CANCELLED\n}\n\nenum LaunchStepState {\n  PENDING\n  \"Started and not finished: running now, or stopped by a fault and to be resumed.\"\n  RUNNING\n  DONE\n  \"Its last attempt failed.\"\n  FAILED\n}\n\n\"\"\"\nA launch (§7.5, §14.6): the engine's job that activates a scheduled change,\nstep by step, each step in a transaction of its own. It begins a minute\nbefore the change's first start; a step that fails is tried again after a\ngrowing wait, and after 5 failures the launch fails and opens an incident.\n\"\"\"\ntype LaunchRun {\n  id: ID!\n  \"The identifier its audit events and log lines carry: launch-12.\"\n  run: String!\n  change: Change!\n  title: String!\n  kind: ChangeKind!\n  \"The version that was approved and scheduled.\"\n  version: Int!\n  state: LaunchState!\n  \"The change's first start.\"\n  starts: MarketTime!\n  \"When it was due: a minute before the start.\"\n  dueAt: DateTime!\n  \"When the engine began it; null before.\"\n  startedAt: DateTime\n  \"When it stopped: done, failed, refused or cancelled; null while it runs.\"\n  finishedAt: DateTime\n  \"The step it is on, or stopped at; null when done.\"\n  currentStep: String\n  \"Attempts of all its steps together.\"\n  attempts: Int!\n  \"Why it stopped, or waits: the last error, the clash; null when all went well.\"\n  cause: String\n  \"When the engine tries the failed step again; null otherwise.\"\n  retryAt: DateTime\n  \"The live catalog snapshot before the launch published, and after; null until known.\"\n  snapshotBefore: ID\n  snapshotAfter: ID\n  \"How it ended, and what people did: published at ..., retried by on-call-1 at ...; null before.\"\n  resolution: String\n  \"Its steps in order: check, prepare, publish, notify, verify. Read through launch(id): empty in a page of launches.\"\n  steps: [LaunchStep!]!\n  \"The sequence numbers of the audit events it wrote (§11). Read through launch(id): empty in a page of launches.\"\n  auditEventSeqs: [ID!]!\n  incidents: [LaunchIncident!]!\n}\n\ntype LaunchStep {\n  \"check, prepare, publish, notify, verify.\"\n  name: String!\n  \"What the step does, in a sentence.\"\n  purpose: String!\n  state: LaunchStepState!\n  \"When its last attempt started; null before the first.\"\n  startedAt: DateTime\n  \"When it was done, or its last attempt failed; null while it runs.\"\n  finishedAt: DateTime\n  attempts: Int!\n  \"The last attempt's error; null once the step is done.\"\n  error: String\n  \"What it found or did: the snapshot it wrote, the offers it published.\"\n  facts: [Fact!]!\n}\n\ntype LaunchIncident {\n  id: ID!\n  kind: IncidentKind!\n  state: IncidentState!\n  summary: String!\n  openedAt: DateTime!\n  closedAt: DateTime\n  resolution: String\n}\n\nunion LaunchResult = LaunchRun | Refusal\n\ntype SubscriberCount {\n  market: MarketCode!\n  plan: PlanCode!\n  count: Int!\n}\n\ntype MarketRevenue {\n  market: MarketCode!\n  \"In the market's currency, without VAT.\"\n  revenue: Money!\n  \"In euros at the declared rate (§3.6).\"\n  revenueEur: Money!\n}\n\nenum AssumptionName {\n  ELIGIBLE\n  TAKE_UP\n  INCREMENTAL\n  RETENTION\n  HORIZON_MONTHS\n}\n\n\"Shares in basis points (1200 is 12%); counts and months as they are.\"\ninput AssumptionInput {\n  name: AssumptionName!\n  value: Int!\n}\n\ntype Assumption {\n  name: AssumptionName!\n  value: Int!\n  \"A default of the business book, or who typed the value and when.\"\n  source: String!\n}\n\n\"Net of VAT (§5.1).\"\ntype Totals {\n  revenue: Money!\n  artists: Money!\n  paymentCosts: Money!\n  contribution: Money!\n}\n\n\"A condition under which finance must sign (§7.3), met or not, with the numbers.\"\ntype FinanceCondition {\n  number: Int!\n  rule: String!\n  met: Boolean!\n  detail: String!\n}\n\ntype Simulation {\n  eligible: Int!\n  takers: Int!\n  stayers: Int!\n  cannibalized: Int!\n  withOffer: Totals!\n  withoutOffer: Totals!\n  difference: Totals!\n  \"Revenue given up on people who would have paid the list price anyway.\"\n  discountCost: Money!\n  \"What the artists' minimum costs the company during the offer months.\"\n  topUpCost: Money!\n  financeConditions: [FinanceCondition!]!\n  \"The lowest retention, in basis points, at which the contribution is not negative; null when none is.\"\n  breakEvenRetentionBasisPoints: Int\n  assumptions: [Assumption!]!\n  horizonMonths: Int!\n}\n\nunion SimulationOutcome = Simulation | Refusal\n\ninput AuditFilter {\n  actor: ID\n  action: String\n  subject: String\n}\n\ntype AuditEvent {\n  seq: ID!\n  at: DateTime!\n  actor: ID!\n  actorRole: ActorRole!\n  action: String!\n  subject: String!\n  \"The request that caused it, from the site or the console through the gateway (§11.1).\"\n  requestId: String!\n  reason: String\n  \"The event's body, as the database's jsonb writes it.\"\n  body: String!\n  previousHash: Sha256!\n  hash: Sha256!\n}\n\ntype AuditPage {\n  nodes: [AuditEvent!]!\n  next: String\n}\n\ninput ChainHeadInput {\n  seq: ID!\n  hash: Sha256!\n}\n\ntype ChainHead {\n  seq: ID!\n  hash: Sha256!\n}\n\ntype ChainVerification {\n  ok: Boolean!\n  events: Int!\n  head: ChainHead\n  \"The first event that does not follow; null when the chain holds.\"\n  brokenAt: ID\n  why: String\n}\n\nunion ExportHeadResult = ChainHead | Refusal\n";

export const publicSdl: string = "\"\"\"\nThe site's API: the public schema of the gateway (business book §2, §4, §6,\n§10, §14.1, §14.5).\n\nIt shows what is for sale and where its price goes, quotes prices and, for\nthe demo's listeners, verifies a student and turns a quote into a\nsubscription. Where a price goes is public, because it is the promise of\n§1.2: the VAT, the artists' share and their guaranteed minimum, what the\nmusic service adds to reach it, what collecting the money costs and what the\nservice keeps. Nothing else of the economics is: no floors, thresholds or\nsimulations; and no changes, versions or approvals, no people of the team, no\naudit. Its whole surface is listed in the gateway's contract test. The price\nis always the engine's (§4.5): nothing here accepts a price, and a\nsubscription confirms a quote by its id.\n\nSigning in is a DEMONSTRATION MODE, not authentication: signInAsListener\npicks one of the demo's listeners, and the gateway keeps which one in a\nsigned, HttpOnly session cookie of the site's own, apart from the console's.\nThe browser never sends a listener for anything else: every call acts for the\nsession's listener. Nothing moves money: the payment provider and the student\nverifier are simulated, and every receipt says so.\n\nMutations need an Idempotency-Key header, except signing in and out, and with\na session they need its CSRF token in X-CSRF-Token. Errors carry\nextensions.code: UNAUTHENTICATED, FORBIDDEN, BAD_USER_INPUT, NOT_FOUND or\nENGINE_UNAVAILABLE.\n\"\"\"\nschema {\n  query: Query\n  mutation: Mutation\n}\n\n\"\"\"\nAn amount of money in the currency's minor unit (cents, pence), never a float.\nWritten as an object whose amount is a string of digits, so that no client\nrounds it: {\"amountMinor\": \"579\", \"currency\": \"EUR\"}.\n\"\"\"\nscalar Money\n\n\"A wall-clock time in a market's time zone, ISO 8601 without an offset: 2026-10-31T23:59.\"\nscalar LocalDateTime\n\n\"An instant, ISO 8601 in UTC: 2026-10-24T07:00:00Z.\"\nscalar DateTime\n\n\"A day in a market's calendar, ISO 8601: 2026-10-26.\"\nscalar Date\n\n\"A market's code, ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 in capitals: IT, FR, DE, GB.\"\nscalar MarketCode\n\n\"A plan's code: lower-case letters, digits and dashes, starting with a letter.\"\nscalar PlanCode\n\ntype Query {\n  markets: [Market!]!\n  \"The plans of a market now, with the price a new subscriber pays (§4.3).\"\n  plans(market: MarketCode!): [Plan!]!\n  \"The list prices of a market, past, current and announced (§4.1).\"\n  prices(market: MarketCode!, plan: PlanCode): [ListPrice!]!\n  \"The offers on sale now in a market: shown if and only if their prices are in force (§7.5).\"\n  offers(market: MarketCode!): [Offer!]!\n  \"The demo's listeners, for the site's entrance: invented people with simulated data. Needs no session.\"\n  demoListeners: [DemoListener!]!\n  \"The listener signed in on this browser, with their account; null when nobody is.\"\n  me: Me\n}\n\ntype Mutation {\n  \"\"\"\n  A quote from the engine for a plan, with or without an offer (§4.5). The\n  site shows it and confirms it later by its id; it expires. Signed in, it is\n  the session's listener's quote, and the engine checks their eligibility.\n  \"\"\"\n  requestQuote(plan: PlanCode!, market: MarketCode!, offerId: ID): QuoteResult!\n  \"DEMONSTRATION MODE: become one of the demo's listeners. Not authentication.\"\n  signInAsListener(listenerId: ID!): Me!\n  \"Ends the site's session; false when there was none.\"\n  signOutListener: Boolean!\n  \"The simulated provider verifies the session's listener as a student, for 12 months (§10).\"\n  verifyStudent: VerificationResult!\n  \"\"\"\n  Subscribes the session's listener at exactly the quoted price (§4.5). The\n  subscription starts at once; its first month's payment comes back PENDING\n  and is settled by the payment provider shortly after: read\n  me { account { payment } } again until it is not. No money moves: the\n  provider is simulated, and its receipt says so.\n  \"\"\"\n  confirmSubscription(quoteId: ID!): SubscriptionResult!\n}\n\ntype Market {\n  code: MarketCode!\n  name: String!\n  currency: String!\n  timeZone: String!\n  \"The standard VAT rate in force, in basis points: 2200 is 22% (§3.1). Prices include it.\"\n  vatBasisPoints: Int!\n  \"What every paying subscription pays into the artists' pool at least, every month, whatever the discount (§1.2, §5.3).\"\n  artistsMinimum: Money!\n}\n\n\"Where a price goes, per subscription per month (§3.5, §5).\"\ntype PriceBreakdown {\n  price: Money!\n  vat: Money!\n  \"The price without VAT.\"\n  net: Money!\n  \"What the artists' pool receives: its share of the net amount, never less than the market's minimum (§5.3).\"\n  artists: Money!\n  \"The part of artists that the music service adds from its own margin to reach the minimum; zero when the share covers it.\"\n  topUp: Money!\n  \"What collecting the money costs (§5.6).\"\n  paymentCosts: Money!\n  \"What the music service keeps; below zero when a price costs it more than it brings.\"\n  companyKeeps: Money!\n}\n\nenum AudioQuality {\n  STANDARD\n  LOSSLESS\n}\n\ntype Entitlements {\n  \"Null means unlimited.\"\n  skipsPerHour: Int\n  audio: AudioQuality!\n  offline: Boolean!\n  seats: Int!\n  needsStudentCheck: Boolean!\n}\n\ntype Plan {\n  code: PlanCode!\n  name: String!\n  paid: Boolean!\n  entitlements: Entitlements!\n  \"Null for the free plan. Prices include VAT (§3.2).\"\n  listPrice: Money\n  \"Where the list price goes; null for the free plan.\"\n  breakdown: PriceBreakdown\n}\n\ntype ListPrice {\n  plan: PlanCode!\n  market: MarketCode!\n  amount: Money!\n  validFrom: LocalDateTime!\n  \"Null: open-ended.\"\n  validUntil: LocalDateTime\n}\n\ntype MarketTime {\n  local: LocalDateTime!\n  utc: DateTime!\n}\n\ntype Offer {\n  id: ID!\n  market: MarketCode!\n  plan: PlanCode!\n  title: String!\n  text: String!\n  terms: String!\n  price: Money!\n  \"The list price in force today, struck through on the page: read from the price list, never typed in the offer (§6.2).\"\n  listPrice: Money!\n  monthsAtOfferPrice: Int!\n  \"Null: no end announced.\"\n  takeableUntil: MarketTime\n  \"Who may take it, in words for the page.\"\n  audience: String!\n  needsStudentCheck: Boolean!\n  \"Where the offer price goes in each of its months (§5); null when the engine does not give it.\"\n  breakdown: PriceBreakdown\n}\n\ntype Quote {\n  id: ID!\n  plan: PlanCode!\n  market: MarketCode!\n  price: Money!\n  listPrice: Money!\n  \"Months at this price; 0 with the list price.\"\n  monthsAtPrice: Int!\n  \"What comes after the offer: the list price in force at that time.\"\n  thenPrice: Money!\n  expiresAt: DateTime!\n  \"Null with the list price.\"\n  offerId: ID\n}\n\n\"One of the demo's listeners: an invented person, and what their simulated data shows.\"\ntype DemoListener {\n  id: ID!\n  market: MarketCode!\n  \"A short name for the entrance: Student in Italy, verified.\"\n  title: String!\n  \"What this listener shows, in a sentence that says the data is simulated.\"\n  label: String!\n  \"The plan they are on now.\"\n  plan: PlanCode\n  \"A student verification valid today in their market.\"\n  studentVerified: Boolean!\n}\n\n\"The listener of this browser's session. DEMONSTRATION MODE: chosen at the entrance, not authenticated.\"\ntype Me {\n  id: ID!\n  market: MarketCode!\n  title: String!\n  \"Send it back in the X-CSRF-Token header with every mutation.\"\n  csrfToken: String!\n  expiresAt: DateTime!\n  account: Account!\n}\n\ntype Account {\n  market: MarketCode!\n  \"The subscription running today in the listener's market.\"\n  subscription: Subscription!\n  \"The first month's payment of the running subscription; null on the free plan, and for a subscription that came with the demo's data.\"\n  payment: Payment\n  \"The latest student verification; null when there has been none.\"\n  studentVerification: StudentVerification\n}\n\n\"A subscription and what it costs, month by month (§4.3, §6.1). Dates are in the market's calendar.\"\ntype Subscription {\n  plan: PlanCode!\n  market: MarketCode!\n  paid: Boolean!\n  \"What each month costs now: during an offer, the quoted offer price.\"\n  price: Money!\n  startedOn: Date!\n  \"The day of the month it is charged on; null on the free plan.\"\n  billingDay: Int\n  \"The offer it was taken with; null at the list price.\"\n  offerTitle: String\n  \"Months at the offer price in all, and those still to come, the current one included.\"\n  offerMonths: Int!\n  offerMonthsLeft: Int!\n  \"From this billing date the list price applies (§6.1); null without an offer.\"\n  fullPriceFrom: Date\n  \"That list price, as the price list stands today; null without an offer.\"\n  fullPrice: Money\n  \"The next charge and its amount; null on the free plan.\"\n  nextBillingOn: Date\n  nextCharge: Money\n}\n\n\"A student verification (§10.2): valid from verifiedOn, until validUntil excluded.\"\ntype StudentVerification {\n  verifiedOn: Date!\n  validUntil: Date!\n  \"simulated: no real student record was checked.\"\n  provider: String!\n  \"Valid today in the listener's market.\"\n  valid: Boolean!\n}\n\n\"A receipt of the simulated payment provider. No money moved: demonstration is always true, and the note says so.\"\ntype Receipt {\n  id: ID!\n  amount: Money!\n  issuedAt: DateTime!\n  provider: String!\n  providerReference: String!\n  demonstration: Boolean!\n  note: String!\n}\n\n\"A payment's state: the provider's answer settles it, each answer counted once.\"\nenum PaymentState {\n  \"Asked for and not settled yet; the subscription runs meanwhile.\"\n  PENDING\n  \"Taken: the receipt is issued.\"\n  SUCCEEDED\n  \"Declined: the paid subscription ends at the end of that day, and the free plan follows the day after.\"\n  FAILED\n}\n\n\"The first month's payment of a subscription confirmed from a quote (§4.5). No money moves: the provider is simulated.\"\ntype Payment {\n  state: PaymentState!\n  amount: Money!\n  \"simulated: no money moves.\"\n  provider: String!\n  requestedAt: DateTime!\n  \"When the provider's answer settled it; null while pending.\"\n  settledAt: DateTime\n  \"Issued when the payment succeeds; null before, and when it fails.\"\n  receipt: Receipt\n}\n\ntype Confirmation {\n  subscription: Subscription!\n  \"The first month's payment: PENDING until the provider answers, then in the account.\"\n  payment: Payment!\n}\n\nenum RefusalCode {\n  \"The offer is no longer on sale.\"\n  OFFER_ENDED\n  \"The quote expired, or its offer is no longer on sale: ask for a new quote.\"\n  QUOTE_EXPIRED\n  \"The listener is not in the offer's audience, or the plan needs a student verification they lack.\"\n  NOT_ELIGIBLE\n  \"A paid subscription of this listener is already running.\"\n  ALREADY_SUBSCRIBED\n  \"The listener already took an offer that does not combine with this one (§10.3).\"\n  NOT_COMBINABLE\n  \"The offer has been taken as many times as it can be (§6.1).\"\n  CAP_REACHED\n  \"The payment provider declined a charge taken at the confirmation, so nothing was subscribed. A payment asked after the confirmation fails as a FAILED payment instead.\"\n  PAYMENT_DECLINED\n  \"This cannot be done here now.\"\n  NOT_AVAILABLE\n}\n\n\"The rules said no: an answer, not an error.\"\ntype Refusal {\n  code: RefusalCode!\n  reason: String!\n}\n\nunion QuoteResult = Quote | Refusal\n\nunion VerificationResult = StudentVerification | Refusal\n\nunion SubscriptionResult = Confirmation | Refusal\n";
